  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The real valued function&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mo>cosec</mo><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>x</mi></mrow><msqrt><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>]</mo></msqrt></mfrac><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> denotes the greatest integer less than or equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo></math> is defined for all <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> belonging to:</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "all reals except integers",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "all non-integers except the interval&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "all integers except <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "all reals except the Interval <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mo>cosec</mo><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>x</mi></mrow><msqrt><mo>{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>}</mo></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p>Domain of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>cosec</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>x</mi></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8712;</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>]</mo><mo>&#8746;</mo><mo>[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>We know,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>}</mo><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;so&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo></math>integers.&nbsp;</p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;belongs to all non-integers except the interval&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></math></p>"
  }
